		"description": "vAPI is Vulnerable Adversely Programmed Interface which is Self-Hostable API Interface that mimics OWASP API Top 10 scenarios in the means of Exercises.\r\n\r\n## Testing against your own deployment\r\n\r\nSet the `host` environment variable to your deployed host (for example `vapi-bdo3.onrender.com`) and use `https://{{host}}/...` in requests. Every folder below also carries plain `curl` commands in its own description, so each challenge can be run outside Postman as well.\r\n\r\n`-s` (silent) keeps curl's output to just the response body. Dropping `-s` in favor of `-v` (verbose) shows the full request and response: the resolved IP, the request line and headers actually sent, the response status line, and every response header, before the body. Use `-v` whenever a call behaves unexpectedly and you need to see what was sent or received, not just the body.\r\n\r\nOnly run these commands against an instance you deployed and control.",
